ork. We see both variations (introduction containing the literature review; separate chapters for introduction and liter
ature review) in our work with students. It’s best to be guided by your own sense of what suits your work and your sup
ervisors’ advice. It’s also worthwhile to look at completed PhD theses from your department, to give you a sense of 
