hor name(s), date of publication, article/chapter name, journal/book/online resource name, volume and issue/edition numb
er, page number(s), place of publication (for books) and DOI (digital object identifier, for journal articles – helpfu
l but optional, as not every article will have one)). For a fuller discussion of these elements, see Chapter 4 , ‘Find
ing Literature’. Make sure to expand the titles of any journals you find mentioned in abbreviated form (e.g. ‘Acc. C
